# =====================================================================================
# Sunrise Dental Clinic Management System
#
# What belongs in this repository is source: Java, SQL, JSP, the Mermaid diagram sources,
# the report generator and the committed evidence of test runs. Everything that a build
# regenerates, every machine-specific setting and every credential stays out.
# =====================================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Java build output
target/
build/
out/
bin/
*.class
*.jar
*.war
*.ear
*.nar

# JVM crash and profiling dumps, which land in the project root
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log
*.hprof

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Maven
# The wrapper jar is deliberately allowed: it is how a marker builds without installing
# Maven first, so it is source rather than build output.
!.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar
.mvn/timing.properties
.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.properties.bak
dependency-reduced-pom.xml
pom.xml.tag
pom.xml.releaseBackup
pom.xml.versionsBackup
pom.xml.next
release.properties
buildNumber.properties

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Test and coverage
*.exec
jacoco.exec
.jqwik-database
surefire-reports/
failsafe-reports/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Node
# Used only by the diagram renderer and the screenshot capture script. Both are committed
# so the images can be regenerated; the dependency tree is a local concern and has no
# business in the history of a Java project.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.npm/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Python
# The report generator runs in a throwaway virtual environment; README.md in docs/report
# gives the one line that recreates it.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
venv/
.venv/
docvenv/
*.egg-info/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ IDE and editors
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.vscode/
nbproject/
.settings/
.classpath
.project
.factorypath
*.sublime-workspace
*.sublime-project
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Operating system
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
*.textClipping

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Logs and scratch
*.log
logs/
*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*.pid

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Credentials
# Never commit a credential. The application reads DB_URL, DB_USERNAME, DB_PASSWORD and
# the mail settings from the environment first and falls back to the blank values in
# application.properties, so a real deployment supplies its own and none reach the
# history. See PersistenceConfig.
application-local.yml
application-local.properties
application-local.yaml
*-local.properties
.env
.env.*
*.env
secrets.properties
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Assessment material
# The CIS6003 brief is the university's copyrighted material. It is kept outside this
# repository deliberately and must not be committed to a public one.
*assessment-brief*
*writ1*.pdf
icbtcis6003*
